title: Hide VCS Metadata From Sandboxes
status: draft
created: 2026-11-21
author: Luke Carrier
items[19]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,"[x] Move the binding vocabulary into the contract","Move `WorkspaceBinding` and `BindingSupport` from `src/vcs/capabilities.rs` into `src/sandbox/contract.rs`, beside `StoreView`. `WorkspaceBinding` has `Copied` and `Bound` with kebab-case serde renaming, no `Default` impl and no serde default. `Capabilities` in `vcs` imports `BindingSupport` from the contract. Update every importer: `vcs/mod.rs`, `vcs/git/scm.rs`, `testing/vcs.rs` and their tests.","`cargo build -p agentkit-litterbox` succeeds with no `BindingSupport` left in `vcs`. `arch-lint check` passes, so the contract still imports nothing internal. A unit test asserts `WorkspaceBinding` round-trips through serde as `copied` and `bound`.",low,"1-2h",,"binding-enum"
  T-002,"[x] Declare the bound root and pin the mask contract","Add `fn bound_root(&self, workspace: &Workspace) -> Result<PathBuf, Error>` to the `Vcs` trait, returning the host directory a bound workspace lives in. Document `masked_paths` as returning paths relative to the workspace root and name `.git` and `.jj` in the doc comment. `GitVcs` returns `Unsupported` from `bound_root` and keeps returning an empty mask. Update the stub in `vcs/mod.rs` and `TestVcs`.","The trait still compiles as `dyn Vcs` and the existing object-safety test passes. `GitVcs::bound_root` returns the neutral unsupported error rather than panicking. No production caller exists yet, so the method is declared and unimplemented, matching `set_tip` and `synced`.",low,"1-2h","T-001","mask-contract,bound-directory"
  T-003,"[x] Carry the binding and the mask in the create request","Extend the contract's `Workspace` with `binding: WorkspaceBinding` and `masked_paths: Vec<PathBuf>`, keeping `source`. The mask is relative to the workspace root, because the sandbox sees the workspace at a backend-specific path. Update the three consumers of `request.workspace.source`: docker, seatbelt and bubblewrap.","`CreateRequest` builds in tests. `cargo clippy -p agentkit-litterbox --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes. No backend reads the new fields yet, so they are present and unused.",low,"1-2h","T-001","mask-contract"
  T-004,"[x] Add the `[vcs]` section and delete `[git]`","Add `vcs: BTreeMap<String, toml::Value>` to `ProjectFile` and `vcs_settings` to `Config`. Delete `GitConfig` and its `snapshot_mode` field. `merge` takes the local file's `vcs` map, notices and ignores the committed file's table the way `config.rs:445-463` already does for `backends`, and extracts `snapshot-mode` from the `[vcs.git]` table into a struct `compose` reads.","A unit test asserts the local file's `[vcs.git]` reaches `Config.vcs_settings`. A test asserts the committed file's table is noticed and ignored. A test asserts `[git]` now fails to parse with an unknown-field error.",medium,"2-4h","T-001","config-key,old-git-key"
  T-005,"[x] Reject `vcs` where it does not belong","Swap `git` for `vcs` in `CONFIG_KEYS`. Add a `vcs` clause to `reject_project_keys_in_user`. Leave `reject_machine_keys_in_local` alone, because `vcs` is not in its refuse list and so the local override accepts it. Extend the loader tests.","A test asserts the user configuration is refused when it sets `[vcs]`. A test asserts the local override is accepted when it sets `[vcs.git] binding`. The old `git` rejection test is replaced rather than left passing on a deleted field.",low,"1-2h","T-004","config-key,project-cannot-set"
  T-006,"[x] Read the section in the composition point","`compose::open` reads `snapshot-mode` from `vcs_settings[\"git\"]` instead of `config.git`, parses `binding` from the same table, and passes `Some(binding)` or `None` to `Sandboxes::with_vcs`. An absent key is `None`. An unparseable value is a configuration error naming the key and the accepted values.","A test asserts an absent binding produces `None` and does not fail `open`. A test asserts `copied` and `bound` parse. A test asserts an unknown value fails naming the key and the values.",low,"1-2h","T-005","config-key,no-default"
  T-007,"[x] Record the binding per sandbox","Add `binding: Option<WorkspaceBinding>` with `#[serde(default)]` to `StoredSandbox`, plus an accessor returning `Copied` for `None`. `create` and `repair` write the accessor's value. `LoadedSandbox` stays unchanged, so a record without the field is still `Current`.","A test asserts a record written without the field loads as `Current` and its accessor returns `Copied`. A test asserts a record with the field round-trips. A test asserts loading never rewrites the record.",low,"1-2h","T-001","record-field,legacy-records,legacy-loads"
  T-008,"[x] Refuse a missing key and an unhonourable combination","`Sandboxes` gains `binding: Option<WorkspaceBinding>` beside `remote`. `create` refuses when it is `None`, naming the key, the accepted values and the file. `create` also refuses when `vcs.capabilities().bindings` cannot honour the configured binding, naming the tool and the binding. `with_vcs` and `for_test` take the new argument.","A test asserts create without a binding fails with a configuration error naming the key and the file. A test asserts `bound` is refused for a VCS reporting `Copied`. `list`, `delete`, `pause` and `resume` still work with `None`.",medium,"2-4h","T-006,T-007","no-default,missing-key-refused,validation,no-fallback"
  T-009,"[x] Branch create on the binding","`create` asks `vcs.masked_paths` after `prepare`, then branches. Under `Copied` it materialises into a `TempDir` as today. Under `Bound` it calls `bound_root` and materialises nothing. Both build one `CreateRequest` carrying the source, the binding and the mask. Every existing failure path that deletes the branch also removes what `bound_root` created.","A test with a recording VCS asserts `masked_paths` is asked and the request carries both the binding and the mask. A test asserts `Copied` still materialises. A test asserts a failure after `bound_root` leaves no directory behind.",medium,"3-5h","T-003,T-008","mask-contract,bound-directory,derived-path,failed-create"
  T-010,"[x] Branch repair on the record","`repair` reads the record's binding rather than the configuration, materialises only under `Copied`, and preserves the binding when it rewrites the record, as `remote` already is.","A test asserts a `Bound` record repairs against its host directory with no materialise call. A test asserts the rewritten record keeps its binding.",low,"1-2h","T-009","record-decides"
  T-011,"[x] Widen prune and sweep orphans","The `prune` call condition at `service.rs:478-482` widens from `stored.remote` to `stored.remote || stored.binding() == Bound`. `GitVcs::prune` keeps its existing bare-clone guard and gains removal of bound directories that have no record.","A test asserts `prune` is called for a `Bound` record even when it is not remote. A test asserts a bound directory with no record is removed. A test asserts a bound directory whose record exists is kept.",medium,"2-4h","T-010","orphans,corrupt-orphan"
  T-012,"[x] Teach the test doubles to mask","`TestVcs` records `masked_paths` and `bound_root` calls and can be configured to report `Bound` support and to return a bound root. `src/testing.rs` gains a masking backend beside `TestBackend` that records the paths it was asked to hide and can be told to refuse.","The doubles stay `#[cfg(test)]` and never become a construction path. Orchestration tests assert the orchestrator asked for the mask and branched on the binding without opening a repository.",low,"1-2h","T-002","gates"
  T-013,"[x] Probe masking a file and a directory","T-002 probed `.jj`, which is a directory. Run a bubblewrap probe twice, once with `.git` as a directory and once with `.git` as a file the way a linked worktree has it, using `--tmpfs` over the directory and a bind over an empty file over the file. Record the output as evidence beside the ADR.","The probe exits cleanly for both shapes and the contents are unreadable in both. If the file shape cannot be masked, the task returns that finding and T-014 records a refusal for that shape rather than leaving a silent gap.",low,"1-2h","T-012","bwrap-masking,empty-mountpoint"
  T-014,"[x] Mask in bubblewrap","`backends/bubblewrap/view.rs` gains masked paths in its render options, emitted after the workspace bind at `view.rs:339-341`: `--tmpfs` over each masked directory, and a bind over an empty file for a masked path that is a file. `backends/bubblewrap/backend.rs` refuses `Bound` when a masked path cannot be rendered.","A rendering test asserts the argv carries a tmpfs per masked directory after the workspace bind. A test asserts a masked file is bound over an empty file. A test asserts the refusal when the shape is unsupported. The existing argv expectation test still passes.",medium,"3-5h","T-013","bwrap-masking,empty-mountpoint"
  T-015,"[x] Probe Docker's empty volume and daemon filesystem","Run a Docker probe for an empty volume at a masked path, both when the bound directory already holds `.git` and when it does not. Separately establish how the backend can tell that the daemon shares the host filesystem, since `compute.rs:630-667` proves only that the connection is a local unix socket.","The probe exits cleanly for both cases, or returns the finding that a mountpoint is not created. The daemon question returns either a check that works or a decision that `Bound` is refused on Docker.",medium,"2-4h","T-012","docker-masking,docker-local"
  T-016,"Mask in Docker","`backends/docker/compute.rs` gains `binds` and `volumes` on `ContainerSpec` and sets them on `HostConfig`, which today carries neither. One empty volume per masked path, mounted inside the bound workspace. `backends/docker/backend.rs` binds the host directory instead of uploading a tar under `Bound` (`backend.rs:365-374`), and refuses when it cannot guarantee the daemon shares the host filesystem.","A test asserts the container spec carries one empty volume per masked path. A test asserts the refusal when the daemon cannot be established as sharing the filesystem. The existing tar upload path is unchanged under `Copied`.",high,"4-8h","T-015","docker-masking,docker-local,no-vcs-data"
  T-017,"Refuse in Seatbelt","`backends/seatbelt/backend.rs` reports that it cannot mask and refuses `Bound` with a structured unsupported failure naming the backend, the binding and the remedy. No masking code is written here in this change.","A test asserts a `Bound` create against Seatbelt fails with an unsupported refusal naming the backend and the remedy, and that no sandbox is created. `Copied` is unchanged.",low,"1-2h","T-003","mask-refusal,cannot-mask-refuses"
  T-018,"Update the configuration reference","`docs/docs/user/litterbox/reference/config.mdx` documents `[git] snapshot-mode`. Replace it with `[vcs.git]` in the local override and document `binding` with its two values and the fact that `create` refuses without it.","The page builds. It names the file the key belongs in, the two accepted values, and the refusal. No reference to `[git]` remains.",low,"1h","T-005","config-key"
  T-019,"Run the gates and smoke both bindings","Run the four gates. Then a manual smoke on a scratch repository: create with `copied`, create with `bound` refused for Git, a legacy record loading and listing, delete removing the state, and `prune` finding an orphan.","All four gates pass on a clean tree. The smoke covers every acceptance criterion that needs a human.",low,"2-3h","T-014,T-016,T-017,T-018","gates,gates-pass,no-vcs-data"
